option.value:
# Character Creation Guide

This guide explains how to create a new character completely independently without needing to ask for help.

## Overview

Creating a new character in your mod requires:
1. **Character Class** - The main character definition
2. **Three Pool Classes** - Card, Relic, and Potion pools
3. **Three Base Classes** - Card, Relic, Power, and Potion base classes
4. **Localization Entries** - Character strings (names, descriptions, dialogue)

The IDE templates have been configured to make this process automatic.

---

## Step-by-Step Character Creation

### Step 1: Create the Character Class

1. **Right-click** the `ShionTheBruiserCode/Character/` folder
2. **Select** `Custom Character` from the IDE templates
3. **Fill in the prompts:**
   - **SHORTNAME**: Your character's display name (e.g., "Alice the Void")
   - **CLASS**: The class name (e.g., `AliceTheVoid`)
   - **CHARACTERID**: Same as CLASS (auto-filled from filename)
   - **COLOR**: Hex color for UI elements (e.g., `ff6b9d` for pink)
   - **GENDER**: Choose Feminine, Masculine, or Neutral
   - **HP**: Starting health (default 60)
   - **NAMESPACE**: Auto-filled - keep as is

The template will generate your character class with:
- Character ID constant
- Color definition
- Starting deck (with placeholder Shion cards - **you'll customize this**)
- Starting relics (with placeholder BattleRags - **you'll customize this**)
- References to your three pools

**Example output:**
```csharp
public class AliceTheVoid : PlaceholderCharacterModel
{
    public const string CharacterId = "AliceTheVoid";
    public static readonly Color Color = new("ff6b9d");
    // ... rest of generated code
}
```

### Step 2: Create Pool Classes

Create three pool classes in the Character folder. You can copy and modify the existing ones:

**CardPool** - `AliceTheVoidCardPool.cs`:
```csharp
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using Godot;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;

public class AliceTheVoidCardPool : CustomCardPoolModel
{
    public override string Title => AliceTheVoid.CharacterId;

    public override string BigEnergyIconPath => "charui/alice_big_energy.png".ImagePath();
    public override string TextEnergyIconPath => "charui/alice_text_energy.png".ImagePath();

    public override float H => 0.9f;   // Customize HSV color
    public override float S => 0.7f;
    public override float V => 0.8f;

    public override Color DeckEntryCardColor => AliceTheVoid.Color;

    public override bool IsColorless => false;
}
```

**RelicPool** - `AliceTheVoidRelicPool.cs`:
```csharp
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using Godot;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;

public class AliceTheVoidRelicPool : CustomRelicPoolModel
{
    public override Color LabOutlineColor => AliceTheVoid.Color;
    public override string BigEnergyIconPath => "charui/alice_big_energy.png".ImagePath();
    public override string TextEnergyIconPath => "charui/alice_text_energy.png".ImagePath();
}
```

**PotionPool** - `AliceTheVoidPotionPool.cs`:
```csharp
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using Godot;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;

public class AliceTheVoidPotionPool : CustomPotionPoolModel
{
    public override Color LabOutlineColor => AliceTheVoid.Color;
    public override string BigEnergyIconPath => "charui/alice_big_energy.png".ImagePath();
    public override string TextEnergyIconPath => "charui/alice_text_energy.png".ImagePath();
}
```

### Step 3: Create Base Classes for Content

Create four base classes that all your character's content will extend. Place them in their respective folders:

**Card Base** - `Cards/AliceTheVoidCard.cs`:
```csharp
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using MegaCrit.Sts2.Core.Entities.Cards;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Cards;

[Pool(typeof(AliceTheVoidCardPool))]
public abstract class AliceTheVoidCard(int cost, CardType type, CardRarity rarity, TargetType target) :
    CustomCardModel(cost, type, rarity, target)
{
    public override string CustomPortraitPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".BigCardImagePath();
    public override string PortraitPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".CardImagePath();
    public override string BetaPortraitPath => $"beta/{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".CardImagePath();
}
```

**Relic Base** - `Relics/AliceTheVoidRelic.cs`:
```csharp
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Relics;

[Pool(typeof(AliceTheVoidRelicPool))]
public abstract class AliceTheVoidRelic : CustomRelicModel
{
    public override string PackedIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".RelicImagePath();
    protected override string PackedIconOutlinePath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}_outline.png".RelicImagePath();
    protected override string BigIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".BigRelicImagePath();
}
```

**Potion Base** - `Potions/AliceTheVoidPotion.cs`:
```csharp
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Potions;

[Pool(typeof(AliceTheVoidPotionPool))]
public abstract class AliceTheVoidPotion : CustomPotionModel
{
    public override string CustomPackedImagePath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".PotionImagePath();
    public override string CustomPackedOutlinePath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}_outline.png".PotionImagePath();
}
```

**Power Base** - `Powers/AliceTheVoidPower.cs`:
```csharp
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using MegaCrit.Sts2.Core.Entities.Powers;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Powers;

public abstract class AliceTheVoidPower : CustomPowerModel
{
    public override string CustomPackedIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".PowerImagePath();
    public override string CustomBigIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".BigPowerImagePath();

    public abstract override PowerType Type { get; }
    public abstract override PowerStackType StackType { get; }
}
```

### Step 4: Update IDE Templates to Include Your Character

Open `ShionTheBruiser.sln.DotSettings` and find these lines (search for "list("):

Change:
```xml
<s:String ... "ShionTheBruiser,SlalTheEndless")</s:String>
```

To:
```xml
<s:String ... "ShionTheBruiser,SlalTheEndless,AliceTheVoid")</s:String>
```

Do this for ALL instances where CHARACTER dropdown appears:
- Custom Card template
- Custom Relic template (also update POOL list)
- Custom Power template
- Custom Potion template

**Example for Relic Pool dropdown:**
```xml
<s:String x:Key="...POOL/Expression/@EntryValue">list("ShionTheBruiserRelicPool,SlalTheEndlessRelicPool,AliceTheVoidRelicPool")</s:String>
```

### Step 5: Add Localization Entries

Edit `ShionTheBruiser/localization/eng/characters.json` and add entries for your character:

```json
{
  // ... existing entries ...

  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.aromaPrinciple": "Lore",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.banter.alive.endTurnPing": "Your turn",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.banter.dead.endTurnPing": "...",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.cardsModifierDescription": "Alice's cards will now appear in rewards and shops.",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.cardsModifierTitle": "Alice's Cards",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.description": "A mysterious character with unique abilities.",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.eventDeathPrevention": "Not yet...",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.goldMonologue": "Gold monologue text",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.possessiveAdjective": "her",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.pronounObject": "her",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.pronounPossessive": "hers",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.pronounSubject": "she",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.title": "The Void",
  "SHIONTHEBRUISER-ALICE_THE_VOID.titleObject": "The Void"
}
```

---

## Creating Content for Your Character

Once your character setup is complete, you can create cards, relics, potions, and powers:

### Creating a Card
1. Right-click `Cards/` folder
2. Select `Custom Card`
3. Choose your **CHARACTER** from the dropdown
4. Enter other details (CLASS, COST, TYPE, etc.)

### Creating a Relic
1. Right-click `Relics/` folder
2. Select `Custom Relic`
3. Choose your **CHARACTER** (POOL auto-selects)
4. Enter other details

### Creating a Power
1. Right-click `Powers/` folder
2. Select `Custom Power`
3. Choose your **CHARACTER**
4. Enter other details

### Creating a Potion
1. Right-click `Potions/` folder
2. Select `Custom Potion`
3. Choose your **CHARACTER**
4. Enter other details

---

## Quick Reference Checklist

When creating a new character named "YourCharacter":

- [ ] Created `YourCharacterClass.cs` in Character folder
- [ ] Created `YourCharacterCardPool.cs` in Character folder
- [ ] Created `YourCharacterRelicPool.cs` in Character folder
- [ ] Created `YourCharacterPotionPool.cs` in Character folder
- [ ] Created `YourCharacterCard.cs` in Cards folder
- [ ] Created `YourCharacterRelic.cs` in Relics folder
- [ ] Created `YourCharacterPotion.cs` in Potions folder
- [ ] Created `YourCharacterPower.cs` in Powers folder
- [ ] Updated CHARACTER dropdown in DotSettings (4 places)
- [ ] Updated POOL dropdown in DotSettings (1 place for relics)
- [ ] Added localization entries in characters.json

---

## Customization Tips

### Character Appearance
Override these methods in your character class:
- `CustomIcon` - Character select screen icon
- `CustomCharacterSelectIconPath` - Character portrait
- `CreateCustomVisuals()` - Battle sprites and animations
- `CustomEnergyCounterPath` - Energy/power counter visuals

### Card/Relic/Power Mechanics
Each base class can be extended with custom logic:
- Override methods to add game mechanics
- Add custom properties for tracking state
- Reference your character's other content

### Color Scheme
Customize in pool classes:
- **H (Hue)**: 0-1 (0=Red, 0.33=Green, 0.66=Blue)
- **S (Saturation)**: 0-1 (0=Gray, 1=Full color)
- **V (Value)**: 0-1 (0=Black, 1=Bright)

---

## Troubleshooting

**Templates not showing up?**
- Reload ReSharper/Rider: Settings → Tools → ReSharper → Rescan solution

**Character not appearing in game?**
- Make sure it's registered in MainFile.cs or through auto-discovery
- Check that pools are correctly named and referenced

**Cards/Relics not pooling correctly?**
- Verify the `[Pool(...)]` attribute matches your pool class name
- Make sure pool class exists in Character folder

---

## Example: Creating "Zara the Mystic"

1. Template → Custom Character
   - SHORTNAME: "Zara the Mystic"
   - CLASS: `ZaraTheMystic`
   - COLOR: `9d4edd` (purple)
   - GENDER: Feminine
   - HP: 65

2. Create pools: `ZaraTheMysticCardPool.cs`, etc.

3. Create base classes: `ZaraTheMysticCard.cs`, etc.

4. Update DotSettings to add "ZaraTheMystic" to all CHARACTER lists

5. Add to characters.json

6. Create cards with: Custom Card → CHARACTER: ZaraTheMystic

Done! You now have a fully functional character.

// ============================================================================
// CHARACTER CREATION TEMPLATE
// Copy and paste this template to quickly set up a new character
// Replace all instances of REPLACE_ME with your character info
// ============================================================================

// Step 1: Save this as "REPLACE_MECharacter.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Character/
/*
namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;

public class REPLACE_MECharacter : PlaceholderCharacterModel
{
    public const string CharacterId = "REPLACE_MECharacter";
    public static readonly Color Color = new("REPLACE_HEX_COLOR"); // e.g., "ff6b9d"

    public override Color NameColor => Color;
    public override CharacterGender Gender => CharacterGender.REPLACE_GENDER; // Feminine, Masculine, or Neutral
    public override int StartingHp => REPLACE_HP; // e.g., 60

    public override IEnumerable<CardModel> StartingDeck =>
    [
        ModelDb.Card<ShionStrike>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionStrike>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionStrike>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionStrike>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionDefend>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionDefend>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionDefend>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionDefend>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionFlood>(),
        ModelDb.Card<ShionBluff>(),
    ];

    public override IReadOnlyList<RelicModel> StartingRelics =>
    [
        ModelDb.Relic<BattleRags>(),
    ];

    public override CardPoolModel CardPool => ModelDb.CardPool<REPLACE_MECharacterCardPool>();
    public override RelicPoolModel RelicPool => ModelDb.RelicPool<REPLACE_MECharacterRelicPool>();
    public override PotionPoolModel PotionPool => ModelDb.PotionPool<REPLACE_MECharacterPotionPool>();
}
*/

// Step 2: Save as "REPLACE_MECharacterCardPool.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Character/
/*
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using Godot;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;

public class REPLACE_MECharacterCardPool : CustomCardPoolModel
{
    public override string Title => REPLACE_MECharacter.CharacterId;

    public override string BigEnergyIconPath => "charui/REPLACE_ME_big_energy.png".ImagePath();
    public override string TextEnergyIconPath => "charui/REPLACE_ME_text_energy.png".ImagePath();

    public override float H => 0.752f; // Adjust HSV values for card back color
    public override float S => 0.779f;
    public override float V => 0.922f;

    public override Color DeckEntryCardColor => REPLACE_MECharacter.Color;

    public override bool IsColorless => false;
}
*/

// Step 3: Save as "REPLACE_MECharacterRelicPool.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Character/
/*
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using Godot;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;

public class REPLACE_MECharacterRelicPool : CustomRelicPoolModel
{
    public override Color LabOutlineColor => REPLACE_MECharacter.Color;

    public override string BigEnergyIconPath => "charui/REPLACE_ME_big_energy.png".ImagePath();
    public override string TextEnergyIconPath => "charui/REPLACE_ME_text_energy.png".ImagePath();
}
*/

// Step 4: Save as "REPLACE_MECharacterPotionPool.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Character/
/*
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using Godot;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;

public class REPLACE_MECharacterPotionPool : CustomPotionPoolModel
{
    public override Color LabOutlineColor => REPLACE_MECharacter.Color;

    public override string BigEnergyIconPath => "charui/REPLACE_ME_big_energy.png".ImagePath();
    public override string TextEnergyIconPath => "charui/REPLACE_ME_text_energy.png".ImagePath();
}
*/

// Step 5: Save as "REPLACE_MECharacterCard.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Cards/
/*
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using MegaCrit.Sts2.Core.Entities.Cards;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Cards;

[Pool(typeof(REPLACE_MECharacterCardPool))]
public abstract class REPLACE_MECharacterCard(int cost, CardType type, CardRarity rarity, TargetType target) :
    CustomCardModel(cost, type, rarity, target)
{
    public override string CustomPortraitPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".BigCardImagePath();
    public override string PortraitPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".CardImagePath();
    public override string BetaPortraitPath => $"beta/{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".CardImagePath();
}
*/

// Step 6: Save as "REPLACE_MECharacterRelic.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Relics/
/*
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Relics;

[Pool(typeof(REPLACE_MECharacterRelicPool))]
public abstract class REPLACE_MECharacterRelic : CustomRelicModel
{
    public override string PackedIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".RelicImagePath();

    protected override string PackedIconOutlinePath =>
        $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}_outline.png".RelicImagePath();

    protected override string BigIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".BigRelicImagePath();
}
*/

// Step 7: Save as "REPLACE_MECharacterPotion.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Potions/
/*
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Character;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Potions;

[Pool(typeof(REPLACE_MECharacterPotionPool))]
public abstract class REPLACE_MECharacterPotion : CustomPotionModel
{
    public override string CustomPackedImagePath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".PotionImagePath();
    public override string CustomPackedOutlinePath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}_outline.png".PotionImagePath();
}
*/

// Step 8: Save as "REPLACE_MECharacterPower.cs" in ShionTheBruiserCode/Powers/
/*
using BaseLib.Abstracts;
using BaseLib.Extensions;
using ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Extensions;
using MegaCrit.Sts2.Core.Entities.Powers;

namespace ShionTheBruiser.ShionTheBruiserCode.Powers;

public abstract class REPLACE_MECharacterPower : CustomPowerModel
{
    public override string CustomPackedIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".PowerImagePath();
    public override string CustomBigIconPath => $"{Id.Entry.RemovePrefix().ToLowerInvariant()}.png".BigPowerImagePath();

    public abstract override PowerType Type { get; }
    public abstract override PowerStackType StackType { get; }
}
*/

// Step 9: Update ShionTheBruiser.sln.DotSettings
// Find these 5 lines and add your character name:
/*
Line 1 (Card template): "ShionTheBruiser,SlalTheEndless" → "ShionTheBruiser,SlalTheEndless,REPLACE_MECharacter"
Line 2 (Relic template CHARACTER): Same as above
Line 3 (Relic template POOL): "ShionTheBruiserRelicPool,SlalTheEndlessRelicPool" → "ShionTheBruiserRelicPool,SlalTheEndlessRelicPool,REPLACE_MECharacterRelicPool"
Line 4 (Power template): Same as Line 1
Line 5 (Potion template): Same as Line 1
*/

// Step 10: Add to ShionTheBruiser/localization/eng/characters.json
/*
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.aromaPrinciple": "Lore",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.banter.alive.endTurnPing": "Your turn",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.banter.dead.endTurnPing": "...",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.cardsModifierDescription": "[Character name]'s cards will now appear in rewards and shops.",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.cardsModifierTitle": "[Character name]'s Cards",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.description": "Character description here",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.eventDeathPrevention": "Survival line",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.goldMonologue": "Gold monologue",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.possessiveAdjective": "her/his/its",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.pronounObject": "her/him/it",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.pronounPossessive": "hers/his/its",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.pronounSubject": "she/he/it",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.title": "Character Title",
"SHIONTHEBRUISER-REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER.titleObject": "Character Title"
*/

// ============================================================================
// REPLACEMENT GUIDE:
// Replace REPLACE_ME with your character name (PascalCase)
// Replace REPLACE_HEX_COLOR with a color code like "ff6b9d"
// Replace REPLACE_GENDER with Feminine, Masculine, or Neutral
// Replace REPLACE_HP with starting health like 60
// Replace REPLACE_ME_CHARACTER with your character name in UPPER_SNAKE_CASE
// ============================================================================
